# Fixed numbers for spaces (workspaces).
#
# herdr numbers spaces by their position in the list, so the number of any given
# space changes whenever one before it is created, closed, or reordered. Pin a
# space here and it keeps that number wherever it drifts to.
#
# Copy this file to your plugin config dir, without the .example suffix:
#   cp space-pins.conf.example "$(herdr plugin config-dir newro.agent-nav)/space-pins.conf"
#
# Format:  <number> = <pattern>
#
# Patterns, in the order they are tried (first match wins):
#
#   @mirror:<host>   a space herdr-mirror is mirroring from that host.
#                    Match by mirror map rather than by label, because a mirrored
#                    space follows the remote's name — "laptop: api" becomes
#                    "laptop: web" the moment the remote switches, and a label
#                    pin would come undone. Without herdr-mirror installed this
#                    simply never matches.
#   @mirror          any mirrored space, whichever host.
#   <label glob>     matched against the space label; * and ? work, and a pattern
#                    without them has to match exactly.
#
# Numbers are free-form strings, so "0" works even though herdr's own indexed
# bindings only go 1..9 — which is the usual reason to pin one.
#
# Examples:
#
#   0 = @mirror:laptop
#   7 = scratch
#   8 = notes-*
